---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Agent Authority & Evidence Audit — BitEvo" description="Bounded engineering audit of AI-agent authority, evidence, logging, traceability and operational controls.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container inner">
      <div class="kicker">Primary engineering audit</div>
      <h1>Agent Authority & Evidence Audit</h1>
      <p>Verify what an agent can do, what evidence exists for its decisions and actions, where controls fail open, and whether the resulting findings can be reproduced from an agreed staging/test workflow.</p>
      <div class="offer">$4,900 fixed · 5 working days</div>
      <a href="/audit-intake" class="cta">Open Rules-of-Engagement intake</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container scope">
    <div class="grid">
      <article><h2>Scope</h2><ul><li>1 staging/test workflow</li><li>Up to 3 tools / APIs / MCP servers</li><li>10–20 agreed failure scenarios</li><li>Written scope before testing</li></ul></article>
      <article><h2>Deliverables</h2><ul><li>Executive report</li><li>Reproducible evidence pack</li><li>Prioritized repair backlog</li><li>One retest</li></ul></article>
      <article><h2>Boundaries</h2><ul><li>Not certification</li><li>Not legal advice</li><li>No guaranteed security or absence of defects</li><li>Production penetration testing not included by default</li></ul></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container method">
    <h2>What is examined</h2>
    <div class="method-grid">
      <div><strong>Authority map</strong><p>Critical actions, tool calls, approval boundaries, prohibited actions and external systems touched by the workflow.</p></div>
      <div><strong>Evidence chain</strong><p>Inputs, approvals, outputs, timestamps, source freshness and logs required to reconstruct why an action occurred.</p></div>
      <div><strong>Failure controls</strong><p>Agreed failure scenarios, safe replay conditions, least-necessary data handling and whether controls fail closed when evidence is missing.</p></div>
      <div><strong>Retest</strong><p>One retest against the agreed finding criteria after the relevant remediation is available.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container lab">
    <div class="kicker">Public-safe internal example</div>
    <h2>LAB-001 — “Healthy service, stale truth”</h2>
    <p><strong>Classification:</strong> INTERNAL_LAB_CASE_REDACTED · customer_case=false · independent_certification=false.</p>
    <p><strong>Pattern:</strong> services looked healthy, but underlying source freshness had stopped advancing.</p>
    <p><strong>Finding class:</strong> false-green observability.</p>
    <p class="small">The public example contains no IP addresses, hostnames, credentials, private databases, customer information or real secret-bearing logs.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container roe">
    <h2>Rules of Engagement gate</h2>
    <p>Testing does not start from a public form submission alone. The intake is used to draft scope; allowed tests, prohibited actions, data boundaries, access approval and replay conditions must be agreed in writing before execution.</p>
    <a href="/audit-intake" class="cta">Open audit intake</a>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hero{padding:66px 0 34px}.inner{text-align:center;max-width:900px}.kicker{color:var(--gold);font-size:.74rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}.hero h1{font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,3.7rem);margin:8px 0 14px}.hero p{color:var(--muted);font-family:'Lora',serif;font-size:1.08rem}.offer{font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:900;margin:22px 0 16px}.cta{display:inline-flex;padding:11px 18px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);background:var(--gold);color:#07090a;font-weight:900}.scope,.method,.lab,.roe{max-width:1020px;padding-block:24px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px}.grid article,.method-grid>div,.lab,.roe{background:var(--paper-soft);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:22px}.grid h2,.method h2,.lab h2,.roe h2{font-family:'Playfair Display',serif}.grid ul{padding-left:18px;color:var(--muted)}.method-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}.method-grid p,.lab p,.roe p{color:var(--muted)}.small{font-size:.84rem}@media(max-width:820px){.grid,.method-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  </style>
</Layout>
